  "worked_solution": "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n(k+3)!=(k+3)\\cdot (k+2)\\cdot (k+1)\\cdot k!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $k!$ and $(k+1)$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(k+3)!}{(k+1)k!}= & \\frac{(k+3)\\cdot (k+2)\\cdot (k+1)\\cdot k!}{(k+1)\\cdot k!} \\\\ = & \\frac{(k+3)\\cdot (k+2)\\cdot \\cancel{(k+1)}\\cdot \\cancel{k!}}{\\cancel{(k+1)}\\cdot \\cancel{k!}} \\\\ = & (k+3)(k+2) \\\\ = & {k}^{2}+5k+6\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
